# Flat Model Warm-Up

Use this notebook to verify that the data loader, graph builder, flat model, and Gaussian loss can run together. This is a short smoke test, not a real experiment.

## Run CPU Warm-Up

```sh
python src/train.py warmup --data data/mabe/raw/mouse_triplet_train.npy --device cpu --steps 5
```

Expected output:

```text
device=cpu
steps=5
initial_loss=<finite number>
final_loss=<finite number>
```

## Notes

- The command does not save checkpoints, logs, plots, or model artifacts.
- Increase `--steps` only when you intentionally want a longer debug run.
- Keep real experiment runs separate from this smoke path.

## Run Flat Training

Training defaults are loaded from `src/config/train/flat_dense_triplet_30fps.yml`.

Inspect the resolved setup without training:

```sh
python src/train.py fit --show-config
```

Start an actual local training run:

```sh
python src/train.py fit --wandb
```

The `--wandb` flag is opt-in. Leave it out for local CLI-only logging. When
`--wandb` and checkpointing are enabled, the best checkpoint is also uploaded as
the `flat-best-checkpoint:best` W&B model artifact.

Override YAML values only when needed:

```sh
python src/train.py fit --config src/config/train/flat_dense_triplet_30fps.yml --device cpu --epochs 5 --batch-size 8 --wandb
```

Resume from the local best checkpoint:

```sh
python src/train.py fit --resume-checkpoint checkpoints/flat/flat_best.pt --wandb
```

Resume from the W&B best model artifact:

```sh
python src/train.py fit --wandb --resume-wandb-artifact flat-best-checkpoint:best
```
